<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Håkon Grjotgardsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 900</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Haakon Grjotgardsson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Håkon Grjotgardsson was a Norwegian chieftain from Hålogaland in the late 9th century, the founder of the line of the Earls of Lade. According to the sagas he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> during the unification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and was made earl of Trøndelag. His descendants, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakon-sigurdsson">Håkon Sigurdsson</a>, ruled much of Norway around the year 1000.</p></div>
